## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/wipe.html
- Summary (EN): Creates a gradual transition between two image sequences by overlaying input b on input a. Unlike the Blend COP, which keeps the layers fully overlapped, Wipe lets the user control where and how they overlap. Output: the transition result.
- Résumé (FR) : Crée une transition progressive entre deux séquences d'images, en Cross Dissolve, Per-Pixel Flip ou Wipe, avec contrôle de la forme et de la ligne de séparation.

- Inputs meaning: ["a: the base layer the wipe starts from", "b: the overlaying layer the wipe transitions to", "shape (optional): controls when pixels switch from one image to the other", "mask (optional): per-pixel mask amount, scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Operation: Cross Dissolve, Per-Pixel Flip, or Wipe (default)", "Amount: how much of the Operation is applied; higher brings in more of b; default 0.5", "Mask: how much of the new value is mixed in; default 1", "Seed: randomness for Per-Pixel Flip", "Shape (Wipe only): Line (default), Rectangle, Circle, 4 Corner Shrink", "Direction (Line wipe): orientation in degrees; default 0", "Filter Scale: anti-aliasing of the boundary; lower values give a sharper transition", "Line Width and Line Color (Wipe only): thickness and colour, with alpha, of the line between inputs"]

- Caveats: ["Shape, Direction, Line Width and Line Color only apply when Operation is set to Wipe", "A wired shape input overrides the Shape parameter"]

